title: Eser Party Conference
subtitle: The PSR chooses their new leader...
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 12 and psr_party_leader = "Chernov"
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/psrcongress.jpg
tags: event
new-page: true

= PSR Conference

The Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries is holding their quadrennial party congress, this year's congress is expected to be divisive, with the various Narodist factions bickering more than ever after Chernov's decision to step down.

The candidate championed by many Liberal-Narodists and sympathetic Centrists is Alexander Kerensky, the former Government Chairman. His election would mark a turn towards a liberalized form of Narodism, something he has been slowly leaning towards since the Eser's turned to the Liberals for governance.

Our ideal Chairman would be Avksentyev, an Eser who is widely respected for being a political moderate. His election would mean a continuation of good relations with our party.

The concservative-wing of the PSR is calling for Dmitry Odinets, a Nationalist, irredentist, and Narodist who has previously voiced his support for restoring Russia's imperial borders.

Then, there is Boris Savinkov, the man who split the Eser vote to provide support Lavr Kornilov's presidential run. Savinkov has attempted to present himself as a pragmatic candidate, pointing to his ties with Kornilov and his experience from the Civil War; short as it was. However, most of the PSR is opposed to his candidacy, as he is considered shady and unreliable.

- @kerensky: Alexander Kerensky is elected as party chair.
- @avksentyev: Nikolay Avksentyev is elected as party chair.
- @odinets: Dmitry Odinets is, shockingly, elected as party chair.
- @savinkov: Boris Savinkov is, somehow, elected as party chair.
- @nomajorityeser: No candidate has managed to secure a majority.

@kerensky
choose-if: psr_right >= psr_left or psr_relation >= 50; 
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Kerensky"; psr_relation -= 5
face-image: img/kerenskywin.jpg

Alexander Kerensky has been selected as the chairman of the Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Chernov, with his history of liberal sympathies. He will preside over a Narodist Party less inclined to compromise with Socialists and more inclined to compromise with the Liberal parties.

@avksentyev
choose-if: psr_right <= psr_left or psr_relation <= 50
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Avksentyev"; rural_rsdrp += 5; workers_psr += 3; psr_relation += 5; pro_republic += 8
face-image:img/avkwin.jpg

Nikolay Avksentyev has emerged victorious in the Congress, and is the new SR Chairman! Avksentyev is a "Heidelberg Eser", a known moderate, and has been influenced by Marxism in the past, the feelings of goodwill between Socialists and Narodists appears to be renewed!

@savinkov
choose-if: psr_right = 10 and psr_relation >= 25
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Savinkov"; psr_relation -= 25
face-image:img/SAVVY.jpg

To the shock and dismay of every democratic party, Boris Savinkov, the champion of a Conservative, Nationalist, and Militarist form of Narodism, has been elected Chariman of the PSR in an upset! The Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries is expected to undergo major internal division, factional divides mend as the party now splits between the outnumbered Savinkovists and their detractors. We should watch his "National-Narodism" closely...

@odinets
choose-if: psr_right >= 10 and psr_left <=5 and psr_relation >= 10
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Odinets"; psr_relation -= 25
face-image: img/odinets.jpg

It appears the Conservatives of the PSR have emerged triumphant, as Dmitry Odinets, a Russian Nationalist and Conservative-Narodist, has been elected party chairman. This, obviously, spells ill for our relations.

@nomajorityeser
choose-if: psr_right = psr_left and psr_relation = 50
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Avksentyev"; rural_rsdrp += 5; workers_psr += 3; psr_relation += 5; pro_republic += 8
face-image:img/avkwin.jpg

Nikolay Avksentyev has emerged victorious in the Congress' second round of voting, and is the new SR Chairman! Avksentyev is a "Heidelberg Eser", a known moderate, and has been influenced by Marxism in the past, the feelings of goodwill between Socialists and Narodists appears to be renewed!